<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        Push notifications (Prompt 5).

        `development` here so a debug build registers against the APNs sandbox.
        Xcode rewrites it to `production` for an App Store or TestFlight
        distribution build, which is why it is safe to commit this value.
    -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>development</string>

    <!--
        ====================================================================
        DELIBERATELY ABSENT
        ====================================================================

        `com.apple.developer.in-app-payments` (Apple Pay)
            Giving implements an Apple Pay path and it is switched off: no
            merchant identifier exists, and `applePayAvailable` returns false
            without one. Declaring the entitlement without a registered
            merchant ID makes signing fail with an error that reads as a
            provisioning problem rather than as a missing setup step. Added in
            one line when the merchant ID exists — see
            P12_STORE_AND_PROVIDER_SETUP.md.

        `com.apple.developer.associated-domains`
            App Links need a verified apple-app-site-association file served
            from a domain this repository does not establish. The custom
            `faithful://` scheme works today; https links do not, and declaring
            the entitlement would not change that.

        Nothing else. A capability is added when a feature needs it, not
        because it might be useful later.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
